Fonts

  The on-screen lettering is baked into the headers below as bitmaps
  rendered from two fonts. Both fonts are licensed under the SIL Open
  Font License 1.1; see assets/fonts/OFL.txt, assets/fonts/OFL-Terminus.txt
  and assets/fonts/FONTS.txt.

  Noto Serif CJK JP Black
    Copyright 2017-2024 Adobe (http://www.adobe.com/).
    Noto is a trademark of Google Inc.
    Used in: title_data.h, zone_title_data.h
    These hold rendered pictures of six fixed titles, not a font, so they
    are covered by this project's own license like any other artwork.

  Noto Sans Mono
    Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors. No Reserved Font Name.
    Used in: hud_font_aa.h

    hud_font_aa.h is the whole ASCII set rendered to coverage maps at the
    one size this program draws them, which makes it a modified version of
    the font rather than a rendering of it. It stays under the SIL Open
    Font License 1.1 - NOT the Apache License above - and is redistributed
    with the license text in assets/fonts. It is distributed only as part
    of this program, never sold on its own. The font file itself is in
    assets/fonts and is needed only to regenerate the header.

  Terminus Font 6x12 bold (ter-u12b.bdf)
    Copyright (C) 2020 Dimitar Toshkov Zhekov, with Reserved Font Name
    "Terminus Font".
    Used in: hud_font.h

    hud_font.h is the whole ASCII set converted to bitmaps, which makes it
    a modified version of the font rather than a rendering of it. It is
    what the interface is lettered with when the world is drawn at 320x240
    rather than at twice that. It stays under the SIL Open Font License
    1.1 - NOT the Apache License above - and is redistributed with the
    license text in assets/fonts. It is not named "Terminus Font", and it
    is distributed only as part of this program, never sold on its own.

